        "id": 3256421
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-20T11:32:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That will not be called after SuspendAudioBroadcast so timer for StopAudioBroadcasts is not set (stop broadcast after 30 minutes). Maybe we should discussed, if we want to stop broadcast during handover at all.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1346,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1346,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "c61cbe52781a7bb1f109c9053706f3452f65e469",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5e0b748c_771a7bf6",
        "filename": "system/bta/le_audio/broadcaster/broadcaster.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1346,
      "author": {
        "id": 1927775
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-21T09:00:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently design allows to PAUSE broadcast. Pause broadcast in my understanding requires some kind of resume, so StartBroadcast is used.\n\nIt\u0027s up to service to \"Resume\" or Destroy paused broadcast. I think the case for timers is when broadcast is not paused.",
      "parentUuid": "be469ab6_37db52b7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1346,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1346,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "c61cbe52781a7bb1f109c9053706f3452f65e469",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f3a1c3a8_ed6732ee",
        "filename": "system/bta/le_audio/broadcaster/broadcaster.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1346,
      "author": {
        "id": 3256421
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-21T09:57:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In short yes. Timers are more for music pause, which will pause broadcast and finally stop it at all. That was introduced for situation that user can forget (after pausing music) that broadcast was started.\n\nWe can skip them in situation of pause caused by handover as then user actively interact with his stuff.\n\nDo we agree?",
      "parentUuid": "5e0b748c_771a7bf6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1346,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1346,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "c61cbe52781a7bb1f109c9053706f3452f65e469",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "08b75531_790bf02b",
        "filename": "system/bta/le_audio/broadcaster/broadcaster.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1346,
      "author": {
        "id": 1927775
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-21T15:16:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes we agree - if broadcast is paused then proper way of handling this would be:\n- Destroy broadcast\n- Resume broadcast\n\nOtherwise it means that device is in Unicast mode and stack should keep broadcast \"paused\"",
      "parentUuid": "f3a1c3a8_ed6732ee",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1346,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1346,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "c61cbe52781a7bb1f109c9053706f3452f65e469",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
